  +# Self-Update Implementation Summary
  +
  +## Original Requirements
  +
  +From **README.md**:
  +- `cpe update` resolves the latest GitHub release, compares it to the baked-in `CPE_VERSION`, downloads the matching binary, verifies its SHA256 checksum, atomically replaces the running binary, and reports the version change.
  +- `cpe update --check` reports the current vs latest version without changing anything.
  +- Automatic updating via `cpe start` checks every 6 hours and auto-installs newer releases; after install, a persistent yellow footer badge (`↑ vX.Y.Z installed – restart to apply`) appears in all TUI modes. Short‑lived CLI commands print a one‑line nudge at most once per 24 h when a newer version exists.
  +- Configuration flag `update_auto?: boolean` in `~/.config/cpe/config.json` (default `true`). Setting `false` disables both auto‑update loops and nudges. Dev builds (`CPE_VERSION === 'dev'`) never check or nudge.
  +- Release integrity: `release.yml` publishes a `SHA256SUMS` file alongside the four binaries; the updater downloads this file for verification.
  +
  +## What Was Built (Phase‑by‑Phase)
  +
  +### Phase 01 – Release checksums (`SHA256SUMS`)
  +- Added `SHA256SUMS` to every GitHub release (`.github/workflows/release.yml`).
  +- Updated `scripts/install.sh` to verify binaries against `SHA256SUMS` when present, with graceful fallback for older releases.
  +- Documented the new asset in `docs/install-and-release.md`.
  +
  +### Phase 02 – Updater core module (`src/update/`)
  +- Implemented `check.ts`, `install.ts`, and `state.ts` to resolve the latest tag via a manual redirect, compare versions, download, verify, and atomically rename the binary.
  +- Added unit tests (`*_test.ts`) covering each module.
  +- Persisted check‑state (`update-check.json`) following the `src/storage/` patterns.
  +
  +### Phase 03 – CLI surface (`cpe update`, config flag, nudge)
  +- Exposed `cpe update [--check]` and `cpe update` commands in `src/commands/update.ts`.
  +- Added `update_auto` flag to `AppConfig` (`src/types/meta.ts`).
  +- Implemented `nudge.ts` to print a one‑line stderr message (`update available: <tag> – run cpe update`) for short‑lived commands when a newer version exists.
  +- Updated `README.md` to document the commands and configuration flag.
  +
  +### Phase 04 – TUI auto‑update loop & footer badge
  +- Created `src/update/auto.ts` which starts a background loop (every 6 hours) that calls the core updater when a newer release is found.
  +- Provided a tiny in‑process store (`subscribeInstalledUpdate`, `getInstalledUpdate`) used by a new hook `useInstalledUpdate` (`src/tui/hooks/useInstalledUpdate.ts`).
  +- Updated TUI footers in `src/tui/Watch.tsx`, `src/tui/Manage.tsx`, `src/tui/Bench.tsx` to display the badge `↑ vX.Y.Z installed – restart to apply`.
  +- Added badge spec to `docs/DESIGN.md` and ensured guards (`CPE_VERSION !== 'dev'` and `config.update_auto !== false`) prevent unnecessary loops.
  +- Tested loop guards and store semantics in `src/update/auto.test.ts`.
  +
  +## Lessons Learned
  +
  +- **Redirect‑based latest‑tag lookup** proved reliable and avoided GitHub API rate limits.
  +- **Atomic binary swap** required downloading to the same directory as `process.execPath` and using `rename()`; this safely replaces the running binary without `ETXTBSY` errors.
  +- **SHA256SUM verification** was crucial for release integrity; the installer gracefully degrades when the file is missing (old releases), satisfying backward compatibility.
  +- **Config flag handling** (optional `update_auto?: boolean`) worked well with the existing `DEFAULT_CONFIG` pattern, defaulting to `true`.
  +- **TUI badge implementation** was lightweight but required a shared in‑process store to persist across renders, fitting nicely with Ink's hook system.
  +- **Testing strategy** – isolated unit tests for each module plus integration tests for the updater loop ensured high confidence before merging.
  +
  +## Next Steps / Open Items
  +
  +- Verify that the auto‑update loop respects the 6‑hour interval under all system states (e.g., suspended, VM migration).
  +- Add telemetry (optional) to report successful/unsuccessful updates for future analytics.
  +- Consider a graceful fallback if the network request to GitHub fails (retry with exponential back‑off).
  +
  +---
  +
  +*All phase documents (`PHASE_0X.md` and corresponding `.prompt.md`) have been consolidated above. The plan folder `docs/self-update/` will be removed as instructed.*
